  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Every protocol endpoint as an MVC controller - authorization, token, introspection, revocation, discovery, keys, UserInfo, pushed authorization, device authorization, CIBA, dynamic client registration and management, end-session and check-session - with routes you can move, JARM and signed introspection responses, and a default cross-origin policy for the OIDC endpoints so a browser client works without extra configuration. Endpoints beyond the core set are opt-in. Referencing both transport adapters is refused at startup with a message naming the package to drop. New in 3.0: the endpoints are mapped with MapOidcControllers, at the routes OidcRouteOptions sets, and serve every tenant of a multi-tenant server. Full details: https://github.com/Abblix/Oidc.Server/releases/tag/v3.0",
